@*
    Audit Definition workspace (Phase 3).

    ONE audit list, and one 3-tab page per audit.

        Audit Definition
        +-- Audit list  (the only list)
              +-- New Definition ------> 3-tab page (create)
              +-- 3 dots -> View ------> 3-tab page (view / edit)

        Tabs: 1 Definition Details   2 Scope Details   3 Question Set

    MODES, ONE PAGE  (2026-11-04: a third, read-only VIEW mode --
      ?definitionId=<id> alone -- shows definition, scope and question
      sets on one page; the 3 tabs below are now the EDIT page,
      ?definitionId=<id>&mode=edit or a ?step= link)
      list   -- no ?definitionId= and no ?mode=new. Only the audit list is
                shown; the tab strip and panels are hidden.
      detail -- ?definitionId=<id> (existing) or ?mode=new (create). The
                list is hidden and the three tabs are shown, all bound to
                the SAME definition id.

    REUSE
      Every tab renders an EXISTING partial, unmodified except for four
      additive hooks in org-assurance-definitions.cshtml (an export of its
      own openDialog/reload, an inline-form flag, a saved event carrying
      the new id, and a View row action). No business logic was rewritten
      and no screen was duplicated:

        Tab 1  org-assurance-definitions   -- its list becomes the master
                                              list; its add/edit FORM is
                                              rendered inline as the tab.
        Tab 2  org-assurance-scope-builder -- its own picker is hidden and
                                              driven by the workspace.
        Tab 3  _audit-question-set-adoption (the 277 link) only.
               2026-11-05: the Question Sets library is no longer hosted
               here -- sets are made on Audit > Question Sets, reached by
               the tab's "Add new question set" link.

    WHY THE FORM IS THE SAME <dialog>
      org-assurance-definitions owns one add/edit form, inside a <dialog>.
      Rather than copy those fields into a second form that would drift,
      the workspace sets window.__oaDefInlineForm and the screen calls
      dialog.show() instead of showModal(); CSS then lays it out inline.
      One form, one submit handler, one validation path.

    CREATE -> SCOPE HANDOFF
      A brand-new audit has no id until the POST returns one. The screen
      now dispatches `audit-definition-saved` with the id from the
      response, so the workspace binds the new audit exactly rather than
      re-reading the list and guessing which row is new.

    2026-11-13 (sir) -- ONE PAGE, ONE SAVE. The three tabs, the step
    caption and Previous / Next are gone. The edit page shows three
    sections one under the other -- Audit Details, Scope, Question Sets --
    each a card with its status chip, and one Save at the bottom:
      1. the definition form   window.__oaDefinitions.save() -> id | null
      2. the scope             window.__oaScopeBuilder.save() -> bool
      3. the question sets     window.__oaAdoption.save()     -> bool
    Three API calls, in that order, not one transaction: if 1 fails
    nothing else runs; if 2 or 3 fail the earlier parts stay saved. The
    outcome -- including each failing section's own error text -- is one
    message box (gracUi.alert), not inline text. The hosted screens' own
    Save buttons are hidden on this page (practice-management.css).
    A NEW audit has no id yet, so Scope and Question Sets say "save the
    audit details first" ([data-new="1"]) until the first Save creates
    it; they then load and the next Save writes them.
    The Scope Builder is Simple only (no Advanced mode) -- see its header.

    543 (2026-11-13, sir) -- DETAILS ONLY. Scope and Question Sets moved
    to Audit Configuration, where each is a step with its own popup. The
    edit page is the Audit Details section and its Save; nothing else is
    saved here. Creating an audit offers "Configure now", which opens
    Audit Configuration on it (the same item as Actions > Audit
    Configuration, encrypted navigation code). The read-only view page
    still shows the scope and question sets: Approved / Active audits are
    not on the Audit Configuration list, and this is where they are seen.
    Submit for Review and Approve moved to Audit Configuration too (542);
    Activate and Retire stay on the Actions menu here.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen

<partial name="Partials/_workflow-common" />

<div class="pm-page-heading compact">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1 id="oaWsHeading">@Model.Title</h1>
        <p id="oaWsSubtitle">@Model.Description</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pm-actions">
        @* 2026-11-04: Actions -- the list row's 3-dot items for this audit.
           On the view page: Edit and the rest, minus View. On the edit page:
           View and the rest, minus Edit. Shared page-actions-menu.js, the
           same button as Gap / Task / Practice View. *@
        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="oaWsActionsBtn" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" hidden>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt" aria-hidden="true"></i> Actions
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-down" aria-hidden="true" style="font-size:10px; margin-left:2px;"></i>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="oaWsBackToList" hidden>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left" aria-hidden="true"></i> Back to audit list
        </button>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="oa-ws" id="oaWsRoot" data-mode="list">

    @* ---------------- View mode (2026-11-04) ----------------
       The audit's read-only view page: definition, scope and question
       sets on one page, no tabs (the Gap / Task View pattern). Edit, and
       the rest of the row's 3-dot items, are on the Actions button. *@
    <section class="pm-panel oa-ws-view" id="oaWsView">
        <div class="pm-toolbar" style="justify-content:space-between">
            <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; align-items:center;">
                <span class="pm-badge" id="oaWvStatus">-</span>
                <span class="pm-badge" id="oaWvVersion" hidden></span>
            </div>
            <button class="pm-button icon" id="oaWvRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="pm-message" id="oaWvMessage" style="display:none;"></div>

        @* 2026-11-13 (sir): the whole audit -- details, every setup step's
           latest status, scope, question sets, workflow, scoring, trigger
           and scope resolution -- drawn by js/Shared/audit-view.js, the same
           page Audit Configuration's "View" shows. *@
        <div id="oaWvBody"></div>
    </section>


    @* ---------------- Sections ----------------
        The definitions partial is rendered ONCE and serves both modes:
        its list is the master list (list mode), its dialog form is the
        Audit Details section (detail mode). Visibility is CSS, by
        [data-mode] / [data-new] on .oa-ws. Each section heading carries
        the 278 status chip. *@
    <div class="oa-ws-panel" id="oaWsPanel-details" data-ws-panel="details">
        <div class="oa-ws-section-head oa-ws-detail">
            <h2>Audit Details</h2><span class="oa-step-chip" data-step-chip="details" hidden></span>
        </div>
        <partial name="Partials/org-assurance-definitions" model="Model" />
    </div>

    @* 543: Scope and Question Sets are configured in Audit Configuration
       (a popup per step); this page keeps the audit details only. *@

    @* The Save for the audit details (2026-11-13). Its outcome is a message
       box (gracUi.alert), not an inline line. *@
    <div class="oa-flow-nav oa-ws-detail oa-ws-savebar">
        <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="oaWsSave">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-floppy-disk" aria-hidden="true"></i> Save
        </button>
    </div>
</section>

<script src="~/js/Shared/page-actions-menu.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/audit-scope-summary.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script src="~/js/Shared/audit-view.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
<script>
(function () {
    'use strict';

    // The definitions screen must render its form inline rather than as a
    // modal. Set BEFORE its boot runs, which is why this flag is assigned
    // at parse time and not inside our own boot.
    window.__oaDefInlineForm = true;

    const API = '/practice/api/org-assurance';
    const U   = p => String(window.appBasePath || window.pmPathBase || '').replace(/\/+$/, '') + p;

    // The page's sections; ?step= deep links scroll to one. 543: details
    // only -- an old ?step=scope / questions link opens the edit page at
    // the top.
    const ORDER = ['details'];

    const root = document.getElementById('oaWsRoot');
    if (!root) return;

    const state = { mode: 'list', definitionId: '', orgId: '' };

    const el = {
        heading  : document.getElementById('oaWsHeading'),
        subtitle : document.getElementById('oaWsSubtitle'),
        back     : document.getElementById('oaWsBackToList'),
        actions  : document.getElementById('oaWsActionsBtn'),
        save     : document.getElementById('oaWsSave')
    };

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Mode
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function setMode(mode) {
        state.mode = mode;
        root.setAttribute('data-mode', mode);
        el.back.hidden = mode === 'list';
        syncActions();
        // 2026-11-04: the definition form is a non-modal <dialog> shown
        // inline as tab 1. Left open outside the edit page it rendered as an
        // Add/Edit card under the list, so close it in list and view mode.
        if (mode !== 'detail') {
            const dlg = document.getElementById('oaDefDialog');
            if (dlg && dlg.open) dlg.close();
        }
        if (mode === 'list') {
            el.heading.textContent  = 'Audit Definition';
            el.subtitle.textContent = 'Every audit in the organization. Open one to edit its details; configure it in Audit Configuration.';
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Actions (2026-11-04). Items come from the definitions screen's own
    // row menu; only Scope is pointed at this page's Scope tab.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    //
    // View page: Edit opens the 3-tab edit page, Scope opens it on the Scope
    // tab, View is left out (this is the view). Edit page: View returns to
    // the view page, Edit is left out. Everything else runs unchanged.
    function syncActions() {
        if (el.actions) el.actions.hidden = !((state.mode === 'detail' || state.mode === 'view') && state.definitionId);
    }
    if (window.gracPageActions && el.actions) {
        window.gracPageActions.attach('oaWsActionsBtn', function () {
            const api = window.__oaDefinitions;
            if (!api || !api.actionItems || !state.definitionId) return [];
            const viewing = state.mode === 'view';
            const src = viewing
                ? api.actionItems(state.definitionId, (view.def && (view.def.currentStatusCode || view.def.CurrentStatusCode)) || '')
                : api.actionItems();
            return src
                .filter(function (it) { return viewing ? it.key !== 'view' : it.key !== 'edit'; })
                // Edit / View come back to this page
                // through audit-definition-open (below), like the list's menu.
                .map(function (it) { return { icon: it.icon, label: it.label, run: it.action }; });
        });
    }

    function toList() {
        setMode('list');
        state.definitionId = '';
        writeUrl({ definitionId: '', mode: '', step: '' });
        clearChips();
        if (window.__oaDefinitions && window.__oaDefinitions.reload) window.__oaDefinitions.reload();
    }
    el.back.addEventListener('click', toList);

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Sections (2026-11-13: one page, no tabs; 543: Audit Details only).
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // ?step= deep links scroll to the section instead of switching a tab.
    // (The Scope / Question Set menu items were removed, 2026-11-13.)
    function showSection(key) {
        if (ORDER.indexOf(key) < 0 || key === 'details') { window.scrollTo(0, 0); return; }
        const panel = document.getElementById('oaWsPanel-' + key);
        if (panel) setTimeout(function () { panel.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' }); }, 50);
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Save (2026-11-13; 543: the audit details only).
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    let saving = false;

    // 2026-11-13 (sir): the Save outcome is a message box. The form reports
    // into its own inline message area; its text is taken into the box and
    // the inline area cleared, so its own later messages still show.
    const SECTION_MESSAGES = [
        { id: 'oaDefMessage',   byHidden: false }
    ];
    function takeMessage(id) {
        const m = SECTION_MESSAGES.find(function (x) { return x.id === id; });
        const node = document.getElementById(id);
        if (!m || !node) return '';
        const shown = m.byHidden ? !node.hidden : node.style.display !== 'none';
        const text = shown ? String(node.textContent || '').trim() : '';
        if (m.byHidden) node.hidden = true; else node.style.display = 'none';
        node.textContent = '';
        return text;
    }
    function clearSectionMessages() { SECTION_MESSAGES.forEach(function (m) { takeMessage(m.id); }); }
    function box(message, type) {
        if (window.gracUi) return window.gracUi.alert(message, { type: type });
        window.alert(message);
        return Promise.resolve();
    }

    async function saveAll() {
        if (saving) return;
        saving = true;
        el.save.disabled = true;
        clearSectionMessages();
        const wasNew = !state.definitionId;
        try {
            const defs = window.__oaDefinitions;
            const id = defs && defs.save ? await defs.save() : null;
            if (!id) {
                const why = takeMessage('oaDefMessage');
                showSection('details');
                await box('The audit details were not saved.'
                    + (why ? ' ' + why : ' Fill in the required fields (Code and Name).'), 'error');
                return;
            }
            takeMessage('oaDefMessage');
            refreshStatus();
            if (wasNew) {
                // 543: scope, question sets and the rest are configured in
                // Audit Configuration -- offer to go there now.
                const go = window.gracUi
                    ? await window.gracUi.confirm('Audit created. Configure it now? Scope, question sets, workflow, scoring, trigger and scope resolution are set in Audit Configuration.',
                        { type: 'success', title: 'Audit created', confirmText: 'Configure now', cancelText: 'Later' })
                    : false;
                if (go) openConfiguration(id);
                return;
            }
            await box('Audit details saved.', 'success');
        } finally {
            saving = false;
            el.save.disabled = false;
        }
    }
    el.save.addEventListener('click', saveAll);

    function writeUrl(patch) {
        try {
            const url = new URL(window.location.href);
            Object.keys(patch).forEach(function (k) {
                if (patch[k]) url.searchParams.set(k, patch[k]); else url.searchParams.delete(k);
            });
            history.replaceState(null, '', url.toString());
        } catch (_) { /* history is a convenience */ }
    }

    // 543: nothing to bind any more -- Scope and Question Sets left this
    // page. Opens Audit Configuration on the audit through the definitions
    // screen's own "Audit Configuration" item (encrypted navigation code).
    function openConfiguration(id) {
        const api = window.__oaDefinitions;
        const items = api && api.actionItems ? api.actionItems(String(id), 'Draft') : [];
        const item = items.find(function (it) { return it.key === 'configuration'; });
        if (item) item.action();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Status chips (migration 278)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const CHIP = {
        Completed     : { text: 'Completed',      cls: 'is-complete' },
        InProgress    : { text: 'In progress',    cls: 'is-partial'  },
        NotConfigured : { text: 'Not configured', cls: 'is-empty'    }
    };
    function clearChips() {
        root.querySelectorAll('[data-step-chip]').forEach(function (c) {
            c.hidden = true; c.textContent = ''; c.className = 'oa-step-chip';
        });
    }
    async function refreshStatus() {
        if (!state.orgId || !state.definitionId) { clearChips(); return; }
        try {
            const r = await fetch(
                U(API + '/definitions/' + encodeURIComponent(state.definitionId)
                  + '/setup-status?organizationId=' + encodeURIComponent(state.orgId)),
                { credentials: 'same-origin' });
            if (!r.ok) { clearChips(); return; }
            const body  = await r.json();
            const steps = (body && (body.steps || body.Steps)) || [];
            clearChips();
            steps.forEach(function (row) {
                const key    = row.stepKey || row.StepKey;
                const status = row.status  || row.Status;
                const chip   = root.querySelector('[data-step-chip="' + key + '"]');
                if (!chip || !CHIP[status]) return;
                chip.hidden = false;
                chip.textContent = CHIP[status].text;
                chip.className = 'oa-step-chip ' + CHIP[status].cls;
            });
        } catch (_) { clearChips(); }
    }
    window.addEventListener('focus', refreshStatus);
    document.addEventListener('audit-setup-changed', refreshStatus);
    // A lifecycle action from the view page's Actions menu changes what it shows.
    document.addEventListener('audit-setup-changed', function () { if (state.mode === 'view') loadView(); });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Opening an audit
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    function openAudit(id, opts) {
        state.definitionId = String(id || '');
        state.orgId = readOrgId();
        setMode('detail');
        el.heading.textContent  = 'Audit Definition';
        el.subtitle.textContent = state.definitionId
            ? 'The audit details. Scope, question sets and the rest are set in Audit Configuration.'
            : 'New audit. Save its details, then configure it in Audit Configuration.';
        writeUrl({ definitionId: state.definitionId, mode: state.definitionId ? 'edit' : 'new', step: '' });

        if (window.__oaDefinitions && window.__oaDefinitions.open) {
            // Same form the list has always used, now rendered inline.
            window.__oaDefinitions.open(state.definitionId ? state.definitionId : null);
        }
        showSection((opts && opts.step) || 'details');
        refreshStatus();
    }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // View page (2026-11-04). Read-only. 2026-11-13: drawn by
    // js/Shared/audit-view.js (window.gracAuditView) -- the definition, the
    // configuration status, scope, question sets, workflow, scoring,
    // trigger and scope resolution -- the same page Audit Configuration's
    // "View" shows. Nothing here writes.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    const view = { def: null };
    const pick = function (o, a, b) { return o ? (o[a] != null ? o[a] : o[b]) : null; };
    function setViewMessage(text) {
        const m = document.getElementById('oaWvMessage');
        m.style.display = text ? 'block' : 'none';
        m.style.background = 'var(--danger-100)'; m.style.color = 'var(--danger-700)';
        m.textContent = text || '';
    }

    function openView(id) {
        state.definitionId = String(id || '');
        state.orgId = readOrgId();
        view.def = null;
        setMode('view');
        el.heading.textContent  = 'Audit Definition';
        el.subtitle.textContent = 'This audit, read-only: its details and its configuration.';
        writeUrl({ definitionId: state.definitionId, mode: '', step: '' });
        loadView();
    }

    async function loadView() {
        if (!state.definitionId || !state.orgId) return;
        setViewMessage('');
        try {
            // 2026-11-13 (sir): js/Shared/audit-view.js draws the whole audit
            // (configuration included) -- shared with Audit Configuration.
            const def = await window.gracAuditView.render(document.getElementById('oaWvBody'), {
                orgId: state.orgId, definitionId: state.definitionId
            });
            if (!def) return;
            view.def = def;
            renderViewHeading(def);
        } catch (err) {
            setViewMessage('Could not load this audit: ' + (err.message || err));
        }
    }

    // The page heading and badges; the sections are audit-view.js's.
    function renderViewHeading(d) {
        el.heading.textContent = (pick(d, 'definitionName', 'DefinitionName') || 'Audit Definition');
        document.getElementById('oaWvStatus').textContent = pick(d, 'currentStatusName', 'CurrentStatusName') || '-';
        const ver = window.gracAuditView.versionLabel(d);
        const verEl = document.getElementById('oaWvVersion');
        verEl.textContent = ver; verEl.hidden = !ver;
    }
    document.getElementById('oaWvRefreshBtn').addEventListener('click', loadView);


    function readOrgId() {
        if (window.__oaDefinitions && window.__oaDefinitions.orgId) {
            const v = window.__oaDefinitions.orgId();
            if (v) return String(v);
        }
        const sel = document.getElementById('oaDefFilterOrganization');
        return sel && sel.value ? String(sel.value) : '';
    }

    // The list's own 3-dot View. Cancelling the event tells the screen we
    // handled it, so it switches tabs here instead of navigating away.
    // 2026-11-04: mode 'edit' (the row's Edit) opens the edit page;
    // anything else (View, row click) the read-only view page.
    document.addEventListener('audit-definition-open', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const d = e.detail || {};
        if (d.mode !== 'edit') { openView(d.definitionId || ''); return; }
        const step = ORDER.indexOf(d.step) >= 0 ? d.step : 'details';
        // Already editing this audit: just scroll to the section (keeps
        // unsaved input).
        if (state.mode === 'detail' && state.definitionId === String(d.definitionId || '')) {
            showSection(step);
            refreshStatus();
            return;
        }
        openAudit(d.definitionId || '', { step: step });
    });

    // Saving the details binds the audit -- including a brand-new one,
    // whose id only exists in the POST response.
    document.addEventListener('audit-definition-saved', function (e) {
        const id = e.detail && e.detail.definitionId;
        if (!id) return;
        state.definitionId = String(id);
        state.orgId = readOrgId();
        writeUrl({ definitionId: state.definitionId, mode: state.mode === 'detail' ? 'edit' : '' });
        syncActions();   // a brand-new audit now has an id
        refreshStatus();
    });

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Boot. Runs after the hosted screens have wired themselves, which
    // `audit-definitions-ready` announces; the timeout is the fallback
    // for the case where this script parses after that event fired.
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    let started = false;
    document.addEventListener('audit-definitions-ready', start);
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { setTimeout(start, 400); });
    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') setTimeout(start, 400);

    function start() {
        if (started) return;
        started = true;

        let wantedId = '', wantedMode = '', wantedStep = '';
        try {
            const q = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
            wantedId   = q.get('definitionId') || '';
            wantedMode = q.get('mode') || '';
            wantedStep = q.get('step') || '';
        } catch (_) { /* ignore */ }

        // The list's "Add Definition" button becomes "New Definition":
        // it opens the blank audit page instead of a modal over the list.
        const addBtn = document.getElementById('oaDefAddBtn');
        if (addBtn) {
            addBtn.textContent = ' New Definition';
            addBtn.insertAdjacentHTML('afterbegin', '<i class="fa-solid fa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>');
            addBtn.addEventListener('click', function () {
                // openDialog(null) already ran on the screen's own handler;
                // this only switches the page into detail mode around it.
                openAudit('', { step: 'details' });
            });
        }

        // ?definitionId= alone is the view page; ?mode=edit or a ?step=
        // deep link is the edit page (scrolled to that section); ?mode=new
        // a blank audit.
        if (wantedMode === 'new' || (wantedId && (wantedMode === 'edit' || ORDER.indexOf(wantedStep) >= 0))) {
            openAudit(wantedMode === 'new' ? '' : wantedId,
                      { step: ORDER.indexOf(wantedStep) >= 0 ? wantedStep : 'details' });
        } else if (wantedId) {
            openView(wantedId);
        } else {
            setMode('list');
        }
    }
})();
</script>
